very, confirm the destination supports idempotency: sending the same request twice has the effect of sending it once. Replay only within the destination's documented scope and time window. Confirm that actions you can't undo don't happen twice. Where support is missing or the result is unclear, check that replay pauses for reconciliation instead of sending again.\n864-\n865-  Why this is hard: Not every outside API supports idempotency keys or a reliable status check. A crash between a successful remote action and the local checkpoint can make replay repeat that action. A local table of past requests doesn't close that gap.\n866-\n867-  If you can't fully do it: Use idempotency enforced by the destination where it exists. Write a durable operation record before sending. If the result is unclear, pause replay and reconcile using the destination's evidence or an operator. Don't retry blindly. Turn off automatic replay for side effects that don't support it, and document that limit. Reject checkpoints you can't verify, and recover from a trusted state. Manual recovery doesn't prove automatic replay is safe.\n868-\n869-  Tradeoffs you can accept: Manual recovery, slower completion, and no automatic replay for unsupported integrations. Never call blind retries of unclear, permanent actions \"safe replay.\" Remaining recovery-control gaps need allowed G2 acceptance.\n--\n881:- **R14.1** Checkpoints and audit records used for recovery are hash-chained or signed.\n882-  - *How to verify:* 1) Find checkpoint and audit storage used for recovery. 2) Check for hash chaining or signatures. 3) Answer no if records are plain rows or files with no chain or signature.\n883:- **R14.2** Recovery verifies them against a key or trust anchor stored separately from the records, and refuses any that fail.\n884-  - *How to verify:* 1) Find recovery code that loads checkpoints. 2) Check it verifies against a key stored separately and refuses failures. 3) Answer no if the key sits in the same store, verification is skipped, or failure is logged and recovery continues.\n885:- **R14.3** Verification catches truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of the whole chain, for example with a signed head or sequence number held outside the store.\n886-  - *How to verify:* 1) Check verification uses a signed head or sequence number held outside the store. 2) Answer no if truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, or replacing the whole chain would still pass.\n887:- **R14.4** Automatic replay sends idempotency keys that the destination enforces, and only for integrations that support them.\n888-  - *How to verify:* 1) Find replay code. 2) Check it sends idempotency keys (`Idempotency-Key`, `client_token`) only to integrations that enforce them. 3) Answer no if replay sends without keys, uses a local dedupe table as the only guard, or replays to integrations without support.\n889:- **R14.5** When idempotency is missing or the result is unclear, replay pauses for reconciliation instead of resending.\n890-  - *How to verify:* 1) Find replay handling for unclear results or missing idempotency. 2) Answer no if replay resends instead of pausing for reconciliation, or retry is the default on timeout.\n891-\n892-### Not covered here\n893-\n894-File these problems under their owning item, not this one, unless this item's own requirement is also broken:\n895-\n896-- What happens to in-flight writes and queued actions at stop → **R12**\n897-- Rollback to an approved earlier release not tested → **C07**\n898-- Agent able to delete or rewrite its own audit history → **E10**\n899-\n900-### Heuristics\n901-\n--\n921:**Needs runtime evidence:** That changed, truncated, rolled-back, and replaced checkpoints are rejected, and replays happen once or pause. Recipe R14.\n922-\n923-**N/A when:** Only when no logs or checkpoints drive recovery and there is no automatic replay.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
